backends/anland: port to the KWin 6.7 RenderDevice API (PowOS)

KWin 6.7 moved EGL display ownership from the backend to a RenderDevice that the
backend owns and hands to its EglBackend (setRenderDevice). Ported the same way KDE
ported VirtualBackend from 6.6 to 6.7:

- AnlandBackend builds its RenderDevice in initialize() from a surfaceless EGL
  display (EGL_MESA_platform_surfaceless) and the DRM render node, or no DRM device
  in ANLAND_NO_DRM_DEVICE mode; replaces the separate m_drmDevice/m_eglDisplay.
- AnlandEglBackend: init() returns bool (setFailed() is gone), createContext() takes
  no config, supportedDrmFormats() returns FormatModifierMap, makeCurrent() results
  checked where a failure means rendering into nothing.
- AnlandOutput: OutputMode is built from an OutputModeline in 6.7 (OutputMode::Flag
  became OutputModeline::Flag).
- core/renderdevice.cpp: a RenderDevice without a DrmDevice skips Vulkan instead of
  dereferencing the null device (needed on Android, where there is no /dev/dri).

Not upstream; lfdevs's patches target KWin 6.6.6.

